## 1. Introduction
Metal–organic frameworks $\left(\mathbf{MOFS}\right)^{1-4}$ are the ultimate designer materials. These novel, crystalline, nanoporous materials are comprised of inorganic subunits (metal ions, clusters, or chains) connected by organic linkers via coordinating groups such as carboxylates, phosphonates, or nitrogen-containing ligands. The modular synthesis approach,5 along with the great diversity of available building blocks and the ability to introduce chemical functionalities6–9 into the structures, provides researchers with
